{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xy2mg8RumaeELX8btT5uUc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CLAUDE.md\n2\t\n3\tThere is no AGENTS.md in this repository.\n4\t\n5\t## Project context\n6\t\n7\t- **Engine:** Godot 4.7.2 stable. `godot/project.godot` declares `config/features=PackedStringArray(\"4.7\", \"GL Compatibility\")`; every log in `logs/` starts `Godot Engine v4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf`.\n8\t- **Renderer:** GL Compatibility. `godot/project.godot` `[rendering]` sets `renderer/rendering_method=\"gl_compatibility\"` and `renderer/rendering_method.mobile=\"gl_compatibility\"`; no `hdr_2d` key. The brief rules out particle trails and 2D particle collision under it (CHANGE-BRIEF.md \"What limits the choices\").\n9\t- **Viewport:** 640 × 360, window 1280 × 720, stretch `canvas_items` (`godot/project.godot` `[display]`).\n10\t- **Effect node types** (CHANGE-BRIEF.md A3, B3, as tuned in Revisions 3, 4 and 6):\n11\t  - Jump puff: `godot/effects/jump_puff.tscn`, `Node2D` root `JumpPuff` with three `CPUParticles2D` children `Flash`, `Puff`, `Specks`, all `one_shot`.\n12\t  - Hose steam: `godot/effects/hose_steam.tscn`, `Node2D` root `HoseSteam` with two `GPUParticles2D` children `Haze` (drawn first) and `Steam`, each with a `ParticleProcessMaterial`.\n13\t  - Both draw a `GradientTexture2D` defined inside the scene; no image file, no draw material (mix blend).\n14\t- **Jump puff event, signal `landed`** (CHANGE-BRIEF.md Revision 2): declared next to `jumped` at the top of `godot/features/player/player.gd`, emitted in `_update_pose()` on the branch that sets `land_ticks = LAND_TICKS` (on the floor after more than 10 physics ticks in the air). `_update_pose()` runs at the end of `_physics_process`, after `move_and_slide()`. `_physics_process` returns at once while `enabled` is false. `godot/game/session.gd` sets `player.enabled = false` in `set_paused()`, in `resolve_contacts()` (DYING, COMPLETE) and in the `menu` handler, so `landed` fires only in PLAYING. `reset_at()` sets `was_on_floor = true` and `air_ticks = 0`, so a respawn never counts as a landing. The player's origin is his feet (`player.gd`: `BOX` comment; collider at `(0, -BOX.y / 2)`). `godot/features/player/jump_puff_driver.gd` connects to `landed`; `jumped` still drives only `session.gd`'s `play_sfx(\"jump\")`. With real keys on `first_steps.json` the shortest landing is the walk-off from the 16 px step at x 160–208: 11 ticks in the air (`logs/test_jump_puff_state_60fps.log`, `walk-off-landing`).\n15\t- **Hose steam condition, `player.hosing`:** `var hosing` in `player.gd`. `session.gd` `_physics_process` writes `player.hosing = water_ticks > 0` inside the PLAYING branch only, so the value holds through PAUSED and DYING. A W press in range sets `extinguish_ticks = EXTINGUISH_TICKS` (240) and `water_ticks = EXTINGUISH_TICKS + 60`. `restart_attempt()` runs from `start_session()`, from the R handler in `_unhandled_input` and from the DYING timeout. It zeroes both counters and calls `player.reset_at()`, which sets `hosing = false` at once.\n16\t- **Hose steam value, `fire_height()`** (`session.gd`): full height (`level.blocking_fire[3]`) until hosing starts, then `full * extinguish_ticks / EXTINGUISH_TICKS`, and 0 once `fire_active` is false. `godot/levels/first_steps.json` has `\"blocking_fire\": [1250, 206, 56, 34]`: base at y 240, centre at x 1278, full height 34.\n17\t- **Pause:** Esc/P call `session.gd` `set_paused()`, which changes only `state` and `player.enabled`. No `.gd` file under `godot/` sets `get_tree().paused` or `process_mode`. `_on_focus_lost()` also pauses, unless `test_mode` is set.\n18\t- **Scene the effects appear in:** `res://game/main.tscn` (`godot/project.godot` `run/main_scene`). It holds one `Node2D` `WalkerJumpman` with `godot/game/session.gd`, whose `_ready()` builds everything in code: solids, hazard areas, `Player.new()`, `Camera2D`, a background `CanvasLayer` (layer −1) and a HUD `CanvasLayer`. `session.gd` `_draw()` draws the buildings, fires and water stream on `WalkerJumpman` itself. The puff's root becomes a child of `WalkerJumpman`, not of the player (CHANGE-BRIEF.md A-R6). The steam root's position is given in level coordinates (B-R4).\n19\t- **Drivers:** `godot/features/player/jump_puff_driver.gd` (a new `JumpPuff` under `WalkerJumpman` just before the player on each `landed`, freed when its three emitters finish) and `godot/features/player/hose_steam_driver.gd` (one `HoseSteam` just before the player; writes its position, `amount_ratio = fire_height() / 34` and `emitting = hosing`). Both are added from `player.gd` `_ready()`, as is `godot/features/debug/vsync_key.gd` (F9 toggles vsync).\n20\t- **Previews (fixtures):** `godot/previews/jump_puff_preview.tscn` (`-- retrigger`, `-- loop`) and `godot/previews/hose_steam_preview.tscn` (`-- loop`, `-- edge_left`, `-- edge_right`), both over the real B1 art, captured as 30 fps strips into `captures/` (CHANGE-BRIEF.md A5, B5); `gpu_price_preview.tscn` plays three phases for the Visual Profiler.\n21\t- **A5 driver pattern:** `godot/features/player/hose_glow.gd` is a `Node` that `player.gd` `_ready()` adds as a child. It reads `hosing` in `_process` and writes one shader parameter. `godot/tests/test_hose_glow.gd` tests it with real key events.\n22\t- **Tests (`godot/tests/`, all `extends SceneTree`):** `_initialize()` defers to `run()`, and `steps(n)` awaits `physics_frame` plus `process_frame`.\n23\t  - `test_game.gd` (41 checks) drives the player through its hooks `test_control`, `test_axis`, `test_jump_pressed`, `test_jump_held` and `test_water_pressed`.\n24\t  - `test_keyboard.gd` (14) and `test_hose_glow.gd` (15) send `InputEventKey`s via `Input.parse_input_event`.\n25\t  - Also `test_audio.gd` (14), `test_materials.gd` (35) and `check_props.gd` (`RESULT: PASS`). Each one calls `quit(1)` on any failure.\n26\t  - Other scripts in the folder: `route_driver.gd` (scripted route), `normal_map_check.gd` (helper for `test_materials.gd`), `calibrate_normal_maps.gd`, `write_grey_strip.gd`, the windowed `capture_*.gd`, `run_check_props.sh` (A3 runner).\n27\t- **Runner:** `scripts/run-test.sh <test-file.gd> <fps|realtime> [timeout-seconds]` runs `godot --headless [--fixed-fps <fps>] --path godot --script res://tests/<file>` under `timeout` (default 120 s). It tees to `logs/<name>_<fps>fps.log` or `logs/<name>_realtime.log`. The exit status is Godot's (124 = hung), or 1 if the log has a `SHADER ERROR` / `SCRIPT ERROR` line. `realtime` drops `--fixed-fps`. It calls `godot` from PATH (on this Mac a local shim; commit `78d926e`) and forwards no other arguments.\n28\t- **Exact commands** (from the repository root; results as in `logs/`):\n29\t\n30\t  ```\n31\t  scripts/run-test.sh test_game.gd 60            # 41/41\n32\t  scripts/run-test.sh test_keyboard.gd 60        # 14/14\n33\t  scripts/run-test.sh test_audio.gd 60           # 12/14 (see below)\n34\t  scripts/run-test.sh test_audio.gd realtime 300 # 14/14 (138 s; times out at the default 120)\n35\t  scripts/run-test.sh check_props.gd 60          # RESULT: PASS\n36\t  scripts/run-test.sh test_hose_glow.gd 30       # 15/15; same at 60 and 144\n37\t  scripts/run-test.sh test_materials.gd 60       # 35/35\n38\t  scripts/run-test.sh test_jump_puff_config.gd 60   # 94/94 (A6)\n39\t  scripts/run-test.sh test_jump_puff_state.gd 60    # 30/30 (A6)\n40\t  scripts/run-test.sh test_hose_steam_config.gd 60  # 89/89 (A6)\n41\t  scripts/run-test.sh test_hose_steam_state.gd 60   # 18/18 (A6)\n42\t  scripts/run-test.sh cost_effects.gd 60 300        # headless CPU price (A6)\n43\t  ```\n44\t\n45\t  `scripts/run-all-tests.sh` runs every line above and prints one summary line per run.\n46\t\n47\t  - `test_audio` fails `music-behaviour` and `music-loops` only when pinned. Both read the music's playback position, which runs on the real-time audio clock (a5/TEST-REPORT.md Baseline). This is pre-existing: leave it, don't \"fix\" it.\n48\t  - New A6 tests run as `scripts/run-test.sh <file>.gd <fps>`. Use `realtime` only for a test that waits on audio.\n49\t\n50\t## Headless facts\n51\t\n52\tWhat a `scripts/run-test.sh` run on this machine can and cannot observe. Probes and logs: `a6/evidence/probes/`.\n53\t\n54\t- A headless run uses a dummy renderer: it draws no particles and runs no GPU particle process. Node state (emitting, one_shot, amount_ratio, visibility, instance counts) is observable; the look is not.\n55\t- A GPU effect's headless CPU price is near zero by construction.\n56\t- Frame strips come from a windowed Movie Maker run, which I start.\n57\t- Measured here (`particle_cost_example09_60fps.log`, Apple M1, `--fixed-fps 60`): `GPUParticles2D` at 1,000 to 50,000 particles costs the same as the empty scene (about 0.004 ms per frame); `CPUParticles2D` costs about 0.055 ms per 1,000 particles and grows with the count. Without `--fixed-fps` every case reads the same ~6.9 ms sleep (Chapter 9).\n58\t- `RenderingServer.get_current_rendering_method()` still reports `gl_compatibility` headless; the empty `get_video_adapter_name()` is the sign that nothing renders (`headless_probe_60fps.log`).\n59\t- A one-shot `CPUParticles2D` simulates headless and emits `finished`; a one-shot `GPUParticles2D` never emits `finished` headless, though `emitting` goes false (`headless_probe_60fps.log`). A test may wait on the CPU puff's `finished`, never on the GPU steam's.\n60\t- `amount_ratio` is set and read back headless; `amount` is unchanged by it.\n61\t- No pixel can be read headless. Every claim about the look is an eye or frame-strip check (CHANGE-BRIEF.md \"Evidence split\").\n62\t- `--fixed-fps N` pins each frame to 1/N s of game time; physics stays at 60 ticks per second, so at 30 fps each frame runs two physics ticks (a5/TEST-REPORT.md: the 300-tick hold took 152 frames at 30 fps).\n63\t- Real input works headless: `Input.parse_input_event()` with `InputEventKey` (`test_keyboard.gd`, `test_hose_glow.gd`) and the player's `test_*` hooks (`test_game.gd`).\n64\t- `test_audio.gd` needs `realtime`, and its last check waits for the 25.6 s music loop, so it also needs the timeout argument (`realtime 300`, 138 s); at the default 120 s it stops at 13/14 with exit 124.\n65\t- A5 shader facts still hold: `Shader.get_shader_uniform_list()` works headless and is empty for a shader that failed to parse; a `set_shader_parameter()` / `get_shader_parameter()` round trip proves nothing.\n66\t\n67\t## Current change\n68\t\n69\t@CHANGE-BRIEF.md\n70\t\n71\t## Ownership\n72\t\n73\t- Files in `godot/shaders/` are hand-written by the human and are never edited by an agent. That covers `hose_glow.gdshader`, `hint_experiment.gdshader`, `hydrant_surface.gdshader` and `standard_generated.gdshader`. An agent may read them, write drivers, tests and scenes that use them, and report what it observes; it does not create, edit, rename or delete anything under `godot/shaders/`.\n74\t- Effect settings live in scene files in `godot/effects/` (`jump_puff.tscn`, `hose_steam.tscn`), not in code. Every value in CHANGE-BRIEF.md A3 and B3 goes in the `.tscn`: node properties, the `ParticleProcessMaterial`, gradients, curves and the `GradientTexture2D`. No driver script sets them.\n75\t- At runtime a driver writes only what the brief gives it. For the puff, that is instancing a `JumpPuff` and placing its root. For the steam, it is `emitting`, `amount_ratio` and the root position (B-R1 to B-R4); `amount` never changes. Only preview scenes set `use_fixed_seed` / `seed`, and only on their own instances.\n76\t- CHANGE-BRIEF.md sections P, C and Q are the human's own words; an agent does not edit them.\n77\t\n78\t## Godot 4 names\n79\t\n80\tUse the Godot 4 class and property names of the pinned 4.7.2, never Godot 3 names.\n81\t\n82\t- **Classes:** `GPUParticles2D` (Godot 3: `Particles2D`), `ParticleProcessMaterial` (Godot 3: `ParticlesMaterial`), `CPUParticles2D`, `GradientTexture2D`, `Gradient`. A 1D gradient texture is `GradientTexture1D` (Godot 3: `GradientTexture`).\n83\t- **Properties:** copy the spelling from CHANGE-BRIEF.md A3 / B3. Every name there exists on 4.7.2 (`a6/evidence/probes/names_probe.log`).\n84\t  - Ranges are `_min` / `_max` pairs. Never write a bare `initial_velocity`, `scale_amount`, `angle`, `angular_velocity`, `damping` or `hue_variation` (prediction P1). `CPUParticles2D` has no `initial_velocity`, so a scene line with it is dropped. `ParticleProcessMaterial` does list `initial_velocity` and `scale`, but only as editor-only range helpers that ignore a number, so a renamed line loads silently and `initial_velocity_min` / `_max` stay 0 (`godot3_names_probe.log`). On `CPUParticles2D`, `scale` is the node's own `Node2D` scale, not the particles'.\n85\t  - CPU and GPU spellings differ: `CPUParticles2D` has `scale_amount_min` / `scale_amount_curve`; `ParticleProcessMaterial` has `scale_min` / `scale_curve`.\n86\t  - The 2D flag is `particle_flag_disable_z` (Godot 3: `flag_disable_z`).\n87\t- **Enum values:** `CPUParticles2D` `emission_shape` point 0 (the default), sphere 1; `ParticleProcessMaterial` box 3 (`names_probe.log`).\n88\t- **GPU-only features:** `CPUParticles2D` has no `amount_ratio`, turbulence or `visibility_rect` (CHANGE-BRIEF.md A3, B3). They exist only on `GPUParticles2D` and its `ParticleProcessMaterial`.\n89\t- **Resource types, checked on 4.7.2** (`headless_probe_60fps.log`): `CPUParticles2D.color_ramp` is a `Gradient` and `scale_amount_curve` a `Curve`; `ParticleProcessMaterial.color_ramp` takes a `GradientTexture1D` and `scale_curve` a `CurveTexture`. Both particle nodes have the `finished` signal and `restart()`. `GPUParticles2D` defaults: `fixed_fps` 30, `interpolate` true, `amount_ratio` 1.0.\n90\t- **GDScript 4:** `PackedScene.instantiate()` (as in `check_props.gd`), `await` (not `yield`), `signal.connect(callable)` (as in `session.gd`), and `process_mode` (Godot 3: `pause_mode`) for tree-pause behaviour. Scene files use `format=3` (as in `godot/game/main.tscn`).\n91\t\n92\t## Out of scope\n93\t\n94\tEffect code is presentation: it reads `player.landed`, `player.hosing`, `session.fire_height()` and `session.level`, and writes none of them.\n95\t\n96\t- `godot/game/session.gd` game logic stays as it is: the state machine, the hose counters, `EXTINGUISH_TICKS`, the 60-tick water linger, `FIRE_DEATH_HOLD`, death, rescue, the timer, pause, audio and input. Esc stays a game pause, not a tree pause.\n97\t- No change to collision, movement, jump timing, poses, the input map or tuning (the `player.gd` physics, `tuning.gd`, `first_steps.json`).\n98\t- No edits to the existing tests or their expectations, including the pinned `test_audio` failures, and none to `scripts/run-test.sh`.\n99\t- The A5 work stays as it is: the shaders (see Ownership), the `hose_glow.gd` driver and its hook, the materials, and the 3D scenes and props.\n100\t- The HUD, the fires and how they are drawn, the survivors, the background and the generated art under `godot/art/` all stay as they are.\n101\t- `project.godot` rendering settings stay as they are, and the renderer is not switched. The Mobile (Metal) price run is a one-off command-line override. No particle trails, no 2D particle collision.\n102\t- The effects use no image files, no additive or other draw material and no `preprocess` above 0, and no steam emits on load. No effect scene fixes a seed. The puff is never a child of the player.\n103\t- The v1 text of `CHANGE-BRIEF.md` is never rewritten; new findings go under Revisions with a date.\n104\t\n105\t## Unconfirmed\n106\t\n107\t- The brief does not say whether the puff and the steam draw in front of or behind Extinguisho: settled by CHANGE-BRIEF.md Revisions 1, 5 and 7 (both behind him).\n108\t- `fire_height()` counts physics ticks (`session.gd`: \"4 s @ 60 Hz\"). B-R3 (\"0.5 after 2.0 s\") is only established at 60 fps; at 30 fps each frame runs two ticks (Headless facts).\n109\t- GPU time on this M1 is reported only under `--rendering-method mobile --rendering-driver vulkan` (`a6/evidence/probes/gpu_time_probe.log`); the Visual Profiler attaches to a normal scene run with `--remote-debug`, not to a `--script` run (a6/TEST-REPORT.md \"GPU price\").\n110\t- `test_keyboard.gd` prints no summary line, so its 14/14 is a count of PASS lines in `logs/test_keyboard_60fps.log`. The contrast figures in the brief are reproduced by `a6/evidence/probes/measure_contrast.py`.\n111\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34beee16-17c2-491e-9181-76b6f2539149","uuid":"8eafcd10-ce13-42fc-92fe-0a93964dd2f6","timestamp":"2026-11-22T20:03:06.312Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/joe/Desktop/repos/walker-ninja-firefighter-joe/CLAUDE.md","content":"# CLAUDE.md\n\nThere is no AGENTS.md in this repository.\n\n## Project context\n\n- **Engine:** Godot 4.7.2 stable. `godot/project.godot` declares `config/features=PackedStringArray(\"4.7\", \"GL Compatibility\")`; every log in `logs/` starts `Godot Engine v4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf`.\n- **Renderer:** GL Compatibility. `godot/project.godot` `[rendering]` sets `renderer/rendering_method=\"gl_compatibility\"` and `renderer/rendering_method.mobile=\"gl_compatibility\"`; no `hdr_2d` key. The brief rules out particle trails and 2D particle collision under it (CHANGE-BRIEF.md \"What limits the choices\").\n- **Viewport:** 640 × 360, window 1280 × 720, stretch `canvas_items` (`godot/project.godot` `[display]`).\n- **Effect node types** (CHANGE-BRIEF.md A3, B3, as tuned in Revisions 3, 4 and 6):\n  - Jump puff: `godot/effects/jump_puff.tscn`, `Node2D` root `JumpPuff` with three `CPUParticles2D` children `Flash`, `Puff`, `Specks`, all `one_shot`.\n  - Hose steam: `godot/effects/hose_steam.tscn`, `Node2D` root `HoseSteam` with two `GPUParticles2D` children `Haze` (drawn first) and `Steam`, each with a `ParticleProcessMaterial`.\n  - Both draw a `GradientTexture2D` defined inside the scene; no image file, no draw material (mix blend).\n- **Jump puff event, signal `landed`** (CHANGE-BRIEF.md Revision 2): declared next to `jumped` at the top of `godot/features/player/player.gd`, emitted in `_update_pose()` on the branch that sets `land_ticks = LAND_TICKS` (on the floor after more than 10 physics ticks in the air). `_update_pose()` runs at the end of `_physics_process`, after `move_and_slide()`. `_physics_process` returns at once while `enabled` is false. `godot/game/session.gd` sets `player.enabled = false` in `set_paused()`, in `resolve_contacts()` (DYING, COMPLETE) and in the `menu` handler, so `landed` fires only in PLAYING. `reset_at()` sets `was_on_floor = true` and `air_ticks = 0`, so a respawn never counts as a landing. The player's origin is his feet (`player.gd`: `BOX` comment; collider at `(0, -BOX.y / 2)`). `godot/features/player/jump_puff_driver.gd` connects to `landed`; `jumped` still drives only `session.gd`'s `play_sfx(\"jump\")`. With real keys on `first_steps.json` the shortest landing is the walk-off from the 16 px step at x 160–208: 11 ticks in the air (`logs/test_jump_puff_state_60fps.log`, `walk-off-landing`).\n- **Hose steam condition, `player.hosing`:** `var hosing` in `player.gd`. `session.gd` `_physics_process` writes `player.hosing = water_ticks > 0` inside the PLAYING branch only, so the value holds through PAUSED and DYING. A W press in range sets `extinguish_ticks = EXTINGUISH_TICKS` (240) and `water_ticks = EXTINGUISH_TICKS + 60`. `restart_attempt()` runs from `start_session()`, from the R handler in `_unhandled_input` and from the DYING timeout. It zeroes both counters and calls `player.reset_at()`, which sets `hosing = false` at once.\n- **Hose steam value, `fire_height()`** (`session.gd`): full height (`level.blocking_fire[3]`) until hosing starts, then `full * extinguish_ticks / EXTINGUISH_TICKS`, and 0 once `fire_active` is false. `godot/levels/first_steps.json` has `\"blocking_fire\": [1250, 206, 56, 34]`: base at y 240, centre at x 1278, full height 34.\n- **Pause:** Esc/P call `session.gd` `set_paused()`, which changes only `state` and `player.enabled`. No `.gd` file under `godot/` sets `get_tree().paused` or `process_mode`. `_on_focus_lost()` also pauses, unless `test_mode` is set.\n- **Scene the effects appear in:** `res://game/main.tscn` (`godot/project.godot` `run/main_scene`). It holds one `Node2D` `WalkerJumpman` with `godot/game/session.gd`, whose `_ready()` builds everything in code: solids, hazard areas, `Player.new()`, `Camera2D`, a background `CanvasLayer` (layer −1) and a HUD `CanvasLayer`. `session.gd` `_draw()` draws the buildings, fires and water stream on `WalkerJumpman` itself. The puff's root becomes a child of `WalkerJumpman`, not of the player (CHANGE-BRIEF.md A-R6). The steam root's position is given in level coordinates (B-R4).\n- **Drivers:** `godot/features/player/jump_puff_driver.gd` (a new `JumpPuff` under `WalkerJumpman` just before the player on each `landed`, freed when its three emitters finish) and `godot/features/player/hose_steam_driver.gd` (one `HoseSteam` just before the player; writes its position, `amount_ratio = fire_height() / 34` and `emitting = hosing`). Both are added from `player.gd` `_ready()`, as is `godot/features/debug/vsync_key.gd` (F9 toggles vsync).\n- **Previews (fixtures):** `godot/previews/jump_puff_preview.tscn` (`-- retrigger`, `-- loop`) and `godot/previews/hose_steam_preview.tscn` (`-- loop`, `-- edge_left`, `-- edge_right`), both over the real B1 art, captured as 30 fps strips into `captures/` (CHANGE-BRIEF.md A5, B5); `gpu_price_preview.tscn` plays three phases for the Visual Profiler.\n- **A5 driver pattern:** `godot/features/player/hose_glow.gd` is a `Node` that `player.gd` `_ready()` adds as a child. It reads `hosing` in `_process` and writes one shader parameter. `godot/tests/test_hose_glow.gd` tests it with real key events.\n- **Tests (`godot/tests/`, all `extends SceneTree`):** `_initialize()` defers to `run()`, and `steps(n)` awaits `physics_frame` plus `process_frame`.\n  - `test_game.gd` (41 checks) drives the player through its hooks `test_control`, `test_axis`, `test_jump_pressed`, `test_jump_held` and `test_water_pressed`.\n  - `test_keyboard.gd` (14) and `test_hose_glow.gd` (15) send `InputEventKey`s via `Input.parse_input_event`.\n  - Also `test_audio.gd` (14), `test_materials.gd` (35) and `check_props.gd` (`RESULT: PASS`). Each one calls `quit(1)` on any failure.\n  - Other scripts in the folder: `route_driver.gd` (scripted route), `normal_map_check.gd` (helper for `test_materials.gd`), `calibrate_normal_maps.gd`, `write_grey_strip.gd`, the windowed `capture_*.gd`, `run_check_props.sh` (A3 runner).\n- **Runner:** `scripts/run-test.sh <test-file.gd> <fps|realtime> [timeout-seconds]` runs `godot --headless [--fixed-fps <fps>] --path godot --script res://tests/<file>` under `timeout` (default 120 s). It tees to `logs/<name>_<fps>fps.log` or `logs/<name>_realtime.log`. The exit status is Godot's (124 = hung), or 1 if the log has a `SHADER ERROR` / `SCRIPT ERROR` line. `realtime` drops `--fixed-fps`. It calls `godot` from PATH (on this Mac a local shim; commit `78d926e`) and forwards no other arguments.\n- **Exact commands** (from the repository root; results as in `logs/`):\n\n  ```\n  scripts/run-test.sh test_game.gd 60            # 41/41\n  scripts/run-test.sh test_keyboard.gd 60        # 14/14\n  scripts/run-test.sh test_audio.gd 60           # 12/14 (see below)\n  scripts/run-test.sh test_audio.gd realtime 300 # 14/14 (138 s; times out at the default 120)\n  scripts/run-test.sh check_props.gd 60          # RESULT: PASS\n  scripts/run-test.sh test_hose_glow.gd 30       # 15/15; same at 60 and 144\n  scripts/run-test.sh test_materials.gd 60       # 35/35\n  scripts/run-test.sh test_jump_puff_config.gd 60   # 94/94 (A6)\n  scripts/run-test.sh test_jump_puff_state.gd 60    # 30/30 (A6)\n  scripts/run-test.sh test_hose_steam_config.gd 60  # 89/89 (A6)\n  scripts/run-test.sh test_hose_steam_state.gd 60   # 18/18 (A6)\n  scripts/run-test.sh cost_effects.gd 60 300        # headless CPU price (A6)\n  ```\n\n  `scripts/run-all-tests.sh` runs every line above and prints one summary line per run.\n\n  - `test_audio` fails `music-behaviour` and `music-loops` only when pinned. Both read the music's playback position, which runs on the real-time audio clock (a5/TEST-REPORT.md Baseline). This is pre-existing: leave it, don't \"fix\" it.\n  - New A6 tests run as `scripts/run-test.sh <file>.gd <fps>`. Use `realtime` only for a test that waits on audio.\n\n## Headless facts\n\nWhat a `scripts/run-test.sh` run on this machine can and cannot observe. Probes and logs: `a6/evidence/probes/`.\n\n- A headless run uses a dummy renderer: it draws no particles and runs no GPU particle process. Node state (emitting, one_shot, amount_ratio, visibility, instance counts) is observable; the look is not.\n- A GPU effect's headless CPU price is near zero by construction.\n- Frame strips come from a windowed Movie Maker run, which I start.\n- Measured here (`particle_cost_example09_60fps.log`, Apple M1, `--fixed-fps 60`): `GPUParticles2D` at 1,000 to 50,000 particles costs the same as the empty scene (about 0.004 ms per frame); `CPUParticles2D` costs about 0.055 ms per 1,000 particles and grows with the count. Without `--fixed-fps` every case reads the same ~6.9 ms sleep (Chapter 9).\n- `RenderingServer.get_current_rendering_method()` still reports `gl_compatibility` headless; the empty `get_video_adapter_name()` is the sign that nothing renders (`headless_probe_60fps.log`).\n- A one-shot `CPUParticles2D` simulates headless and emits `finished`; a one-shot `GPUParticles2D` never emits `finished` headless, though `emitting` goes false (`headless_probe_60fps.log`). A test may wait on the CPU puff's `finished`, never on the GPU steam's.\n- `amount_ratio` is set and read back headless; `amount` is unchanged by it.\n- No pixel can be read headless. Every claim about the look is an eye or frame-strip check (CHANGE-BRIEF.md \"Evidence split\").\n- `--fixed-fps N` pins each frame to 1/N s of game time; physics stays at 60 ticks per second, so at 30 fps each frame runs two physics ticks (a5/TEST-REPORT.md: the 300-tick hold took 152 frames at 30 fps).\n- Real input works headless: `Input.parse_input_event()` with `InputEventKey` (`test_keyboard.gd`, `test_hose_glow.gd`) and the player's `test_*` hooks (`test_game.gd`).\n- `test_audio.gd` needs `realtime`, and its last check waits for the 25.6 s music loop, so it also needs the timeout argument (`realtime 300`, 138 s); at the default 120 s it stops at 13/14 with exit 124.\n- A5 shader facts still hold: `Shader.get_shader_uniform_list()` works headless and is empty for a shader that failed to parse; a `set_shader_parameter()` / `get_shader_parameter()` round trip proves nothing.\n\n## Current change\n\n@CHANGE-BRIEF.md\n\n## Ownership\n\n- Files in `godot/shaders/` are hand-written by the human and are never edited by an agent. That covers `hose_glow.gdshader`, `hint_experiment.gdshader`, `hydrant_surface.gdshader` and `standard_generated.gdshader`. An agent may read them, write drivers, tests and scenes that use them, and report what it observes; it does not create, edit, rename or delete anything under `godot/shaders/`.\n- Effect settings live in scene files in `godot/effects/` (`jump_puff.tscn`, `hose_steam.tscn`), not in code. Every value in CHANGE-BRIEF.md A3 and B3 goes in the `.tscn`: node properties, the `ParticleProcessMaterial`, gradients, curves and the `GradientTexture2D`. No driver script sets them.\n- At runtime a driver writes only what the brief gives it. For the puff, that is instancing a `JumpPuff` and placing its root. For the steam, it is `emitting`, `amount_ratio` and the root position (B-R1 to B-R4); `amount` never changes. Only preview scenes set `use_fixed_seed` / `seed`, and only on their own instances.\n- CHANGE-BRIEF.md sections P, C and Q are the human's own words; an agent does not edit them.\n\n## Godot 4 names\n\nUse the Godot 4 class and property names of the pinned 4.7.2, never Godot 3 names.\n\n- **Classes:** `GPUParticles2D` (Godot 3: `Particles2D`), `ParticleProcessMaterial` (Godot 3: `ParticlesMaterial`), `CPUParticles2D`, `GradientTexture2D`, `Gradient`. A 1D gradient texture is `GradientTexture1D` (Godot 3: `GradientTexture`).\n- **Properties:** copy the spelling from CHANGE-BRIEF.md A3 / B3. Every name there exists on 4.7.2 (`a6/evidence/probes/names_probe.log`).\n  - Ranges are `_min` / `_max` pairs. Never write a bare `initial_velocity`, `scale_amount`, `angle`, `angular_velocity`, `damping` or `hue_variation` (prediction P1). `CPUParticles2D` has no `initial_velocity`, so a scene line with it is dropped. `ParticleProcessMaterial` does list `initial_velocity` and `scale`, but only as editor-only range helpers that ignore a number, so a renamed line loads silently and `initial_velocity_min` / `_max` stay 0 (`godot3_names_probe.log`). On `CPUParticles2D`, `scale` is the node's own `Node2D` scale, not the particles'.\n  - CPU and GPU spellings differ: `CPUParticles2D` has `scale_amount_min` / `scale_amount_curve`; `ParticleProcessMaterial` has `scale_min` / `scale_curve`.\n  - The 2D flag is `particle_flag_disable_z` (Godot 3: `flag_disable_z`).\n- **Enum values:** `CPUParticles2D` `emission_shape` point 0 (the default), sphere 1; `ParticleProcessMaterial` box 3 (`names_probe.log`).\n- **GPU-only features:** `CPUParticles2D` has no `amount_ratio`, turbulence or `visibility_rect` (CHANGE-BRIEF.md A3, B3). They exist only on `GPUParticles2D` and its `ParticleProcessMaterial`.\n- **Resource types, checked on 4.7.2** (`headless_probe_60fps.log`): `CPUParticles2D.color_ramp` is a `Gradient` and `scale_amount_curve` a `Curve`; `ParticleProcessMaterial.color_ramp` takes a `GradientTexture1D` and `scale_curve` a `CurveTexture`. Both particle nodes have the `finished` signal and `restart()`. `GPUParticles2D` defaults: `fixed_fps` 30, `interpolate` true, `amount_ratio` 1.0.\n- **GDScript 4:** `PackedScene.instantiate()` (as in `check_props.gd`), `await` (not `yield`), `signal.connect(callable)` (as in `session.gd`), and `process_mode` (Godot 3: `pause_mode`) for tree-pause behaviour. Scene files use `format=3` (as in `godot/game/main.tscn`).\n\n## Out of scope\n\nEffect code is presentation: it reads `player.landed`, `player.hosing`, `session.fire_height()` and `session.level`, and writes none of them.\n\n- `godot/game/session.gd` game logic stays as it is: the state machine, the hose counters, `EXTINGUISH_TICKS`, the 60-tick water linger, `FIRE_DEATH_HOLD`, death, rescue, the timer, pause, audio and input. Esc stays a game pause, not a tree pause.\n- No change to collision, movement, jump timing, poses, the input map or tuning (the `player.gd` physics, `tuning.gd`, `first_steps.json`).\n- No edits to the existing tests or their expectations, including the pinned `test_audio` failures, and none to `scripts/run-test.sh`.\n- The A5 work stays as it is: the shaders (see Ownership), the `hose_glow.gd` driver and its hook, the materials, and the 3D scenes and props.\n- The HUD, the fires and how they are drawn, the survivors, the background and the generated art under `godot/art/` all stay as they are.\n- `project.godot` rendering settings stay as they are, and the renderer is not switched. The Mobile (Metal) price run is a one-off command-line override. No particle trails, no 2D particle collision.\n- The effects use no image files, no additive or other draw material and no `preprocess` above 0, and no steam emits on load. No effect scene fixes a seed. The puff is never a child of the player.\n- The v1 text of `CHANGE-BRIEF.md` is never rewritten; new findings go under Revisions with a date.\n\n## Unconfirmed\n\n- The brief does not say whether the puff and the steam draw in front of or behind Extinguisho: settled by CHANGE-BRIEF.md Revisions 1, 5 and 7 (both behind him).\n- `fire_height()` counts physics ticks (`session.gd`: \"4 s @ 60 Hz\"). B-R3 (\"0.5 after 2.0 s\") is only established at 60 fps; at 30 fps each frame runs two ticks (Headless facts).\n- GPU time on this M1 is reported only under `--rendering-method mobile --rendering-driver vulkan` (`a6/evidence/probes/gpu_time_probe.log`); the Visual Profiler attaches to a normal scene run with `--remote-debug`, not to a `--script` run (a6/TEST-REPORT.md \"GPU price\").\n- `test_keyboard.gd` prints no summary line, so its 14/14 is a count of PASS lines in `logs/test_keyboard_60fps.log`. The contrast figures in the brief are reproduced by `a6/evidence/probes/measure_contrast.py`.\n","numLines":111,"startLine":1,"totalLines":111}}}
