{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DBt3L7XT3VTJK6VskJktHN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\textends Node\n2\t# Hose glow driver (CHANGE-BRIEF A2/A3, Revision 3). Presentation only: it reads player.hosing\n3\t# and writes one shader parameter on player.sprite. It never writes game state.\n4\t\n5\tconst SHADER := preload(\"res://shaders/hose_glow.gdshader\")  # hand-written; not edited here\n6\tconst PARAM := \"glow\"\n7\tconst RAMP_SECONDS := 0.25   # R3: the ramps move at 1/RAMP_SECONDS per game second (0 -> 1 in 0.25 s)\n8\tconst BREATH_CENTRE := 0.6   # Revision 3: while hosing, glow breathes 0.4..0.8 ...\n9\tconst BREATH_AMPLITUDE := 0.2\n10\tconst BREATH_PERIOD := 1.0   # ... with a 1.0 s period, in game seconds\n11\tvar glow := 0.0\n12\tvar hose_time := 0.0         # game seconds since hosing began (driver clock, not the shader's TIME)\n13\tvar material: ShaderMaterial\n14\t\n15\tfunc _ready() -> void:\n16\t\tname = \"HoseGlow\"\n17\t\t# One material per player instance (R8), on the sprite only (F5): the code-drawn rescue\n18\t\t# bag and survivor heads are drawn on the body, not on the sprite, so they keep their colours.\n19\t\tmaterial = ShaderMaterial.new()\n20\t\tmaterial.shader = SHADER\n21\t\tget_parent().sprite.material = material\n22\t\tmaterial.set_shader_parameter(PARAM, glow)\n23\t\n24\tfunc _process(delta: float) -> void:\n25\t\t# _process runs after this frame's physics ticks, so it sees the session's fresh `hosing`.\n26\t\t# delta is scaled game time (R4, R6): the ramps and the breathing run on it at any frame rate.\n27\t\t# move_toward from the current value: a state change mid-ramp reverses from where it is (R7).\n28\t\tvar target := 0.0\n29\t\tif get_parent().hosing:\n30\t\t\t# t = 0 on the first frame hosing is seen (target 0.6), then accumulates per frame.\n31\t\t\ttarget = BREATH_CENTRE + BREATH_AMPLITUDE * sin(TAU * hose_time / BREATH_PERIOD)\n32\t\t\those_time += delta\n33\t\telse:\n34\t\t\those_time = 0.0\n35\t\tglow = move_toward(glow, target, delta / RAMP_SECONDS)\n36\t\tmaterial.set_shader_parameter(PARAM, glow)\n37\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34beee16-17c2-491e-9181-76b6f2539149","uuid":"3f4ebe91-789a-4d19-8005-eb8820c787a7","timestamp":"2026-11-22T20:03:28.719Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/joe/Desktop/repos/walker-ninja-firefighter-joe/godot/features/player/hose_glow.gd","content":"extends Node\n# Hose glow driver (CHANGE-BRIEF A2/A3, Revision 3). Presentation only: it reads player.hosing\n# and writes one shader parameter on player.sprite. It never writes game state.\n\nconst SHADER := preload(\"res://shaders/hose_glow.gdshader\")  # hand-written; not edited here\nconst PARAM := \"glow\"\nconst RAMP_SECONDS := 0.25   # R3: the ramps move at 1/RAMP_SECONDS per game second (0 -> 1 in 0.25 s)\nconst BREATH_CENTRE := 0.6   # Revision 3: while hosing, glow breathes 0.4..0.8 ...\nconst BREATH_AMPLITUDE := 0.2\nconst BREATH_PERIOD := 1.0   # ... with a 1.0 s period, in game seconds\nvar glow := 0.0\nvar hose_time := 0.0         # game seconds since hosing began (driver clock, not the shader's TIME)\nvar material: ShaderMaterial\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tname = \"HoseGlow\"\n\t# One material per player instance (R8), on the sprite only (F5): the code-drawn rescue\n\t# bag and survivor heads are drawn on the body, not on the sprite, so they keep their colours.\n\tmaterial = ShaderMaterial.new()\n\tmaterial.shader = SHADER\n\tget_parent().sprite.material = material\n\tmaterial.set_shader_parameter(PARAM, glow)\n\nfunc _process(delta: float) -> void:\n\t# _process runs after this frame's physics ticks, so it sees the session's fresh `hosing`.\n\t# delta is scaled game time (R4, R6): the ramps and the breathing run on it at any frame rate.\n\t# move_toward from the current value: a state change mid-ramp reverses from where it is (R7).\n\tvar target := 0.0\n\tif get_parent().hosing:\n\t\t# t = 0 on the first frame hosing is seen (target 0.6), then accumulates per frame.\n\t\ttarget = BREATH_CENTRE + BREATH_AMPLITUDE * sin(TAU * hose_time / BREATH_PERIOD)\n\t\those_time += delta\n\telse:\n\t\those_time = 0.0\n\tglow = move_toward(glow, target, delta / RAMP_SECONDS)\n\tmaterial.set_shader_parameter(PARAM, glow)\n","numLines":37,"startLine":1,"totalLines":37}}}
